    "title": "Anthony Bowens Joined AEW Due To Its LGBTQ+ Representation, ROH TV On HonorClub **SPOILERS** - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n1 hours ago\nAnthony Bowens recently reflected on his decision to join AEW, noting that the promotion’s LGBTQ+ representation was an important factor in signing.\nBowens, who came on board in late 2020, spoke about his experience and what attracted him to the company in a new interview with Jimmy V3. He said,\n“I didn’t have much representation when I was growing up watching wrestling,” Bowens said. “I mean, there was maybe one, two, if that. But it’s really cool to be able to live my dream and also have people relate to your story and have people relate to your journey and know that you’re impacting folks positively just by living your dream.”\nREAD MORE: Mini Mone Officially Returns To AEW, Orange Cassidy Reacts To His Time Off, & Lots More\nREAD MORE: The Justice League Goes #AllElite, AEW Stars Enter DC Universe – Details\nHe continued, “It’s been great working at AEW because I always feel free to be myself. It was never a worry. As a matter of fact, that was one of the contributing factors to coming here in the first place was when I was first a extra here, I just noticed people like Sonny Kiss and Nyla Rose walking around not worrying about anything, judgment-free. being able to live their lives normally like everything should be. So it’s a great environment to work in, an environment where I’ve always been able to be myself, which I’m super grateful for.”\nPrior to this week’s episode of AEW Dynamite, the following matches were taped for an upcoming episode of ROH TV on HonorClub:\n* Keagan Garland def. Jon Cruz\n* Alex Windsor & Sareee def. Diamante & Billie Starkz\n* HOOK def. Aaron Solo",
